@startuml STREAMSat_Pipeline
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam arrowThickness 2

title STREAM-Sat — Ensemble Precipitation Pipeline

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' PIPELINE FLOW (left to right)
' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

rectangle "  IMERG Early Run\n  30-min, 0.1° QPE  " as imerg #BBDEFB
rectangle "  GFS 850 hPa\n  U/V Wind Components  " as gfs #BBDEFB
rectangle "  CSGD Error Model\n  (pre-trained, per-pixel)  " as csgd #E1BEE7

rectangle "  Convert Winds\n  GFS U/V → Motion Vectors\n  (speed + direction)  " as mv #FFF9C4
rectangle "  Noise Generation\n  anisotropic, non-stationary\n  50 ensemble members\n  (STREAM_NoiseGeneration.py)  " as noise #FFE0B2
rectangle "  Precip Simulation\n  CSGD error model + IMERG\n  50 ensemble members\n  (STREAM_PrecipSimulation.py)  " as sim #FFCCBC
rectangle "  NetCDF Ensemble Output\n  48h window, half-hourly\n  1 file = 50 members × 96 steps\n  → converted to GeoTIFFs per member  " as out #C8E6C9

' ── Flow arrows ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
imerg -down-> mv
gfs -down-> mv
csgd --> sim
mv -down-> noise
noise -down-> sim
sim -down-> out

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' TIMELINE: FIRST CYCLE vs SUBSEQUENT CYCLES
' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

note right of out
  **FIRST CYCLE (Cold Start)**
  ─────────────────────────
  • No saved state found → cold start
  • Ingest window: **60 hours**
    (48h output + 12h AR(1) warm-up)
  • Generate noise for all 60h
  • Run 50 ensemble members (~3-4 min)
  • Trim: drop first **24 half-hourly steps**
    (= 12h AR(1) warm-up buffer)
  • Output: **96 new timesteps written**
    (48h @ 30-min)
  • Save state: last 12 timesteps × 50 members
    → state_caribbean.pkl (~50 MB)
  **SUCCESS** → STREAMSat_..._Ens50.nc
end note

note right of out #F5F5F5
  **SUBSEQUENT CYCLES (+30 min)**
  ───────────────────────────────
  • Load saved state from previous cycle
    → **override** first 12 noise timesteps
    per member → bit-identical members
  • Ingest window: **60 hours** (shifted +30 min)
  • Run 50 ensemble members (~3-4 min)
  • Trim: drop first 24 steps (12h warm-up)
  • Output: **1 new timestep** written,
    **95 skipped** (already exist)
  • Save state: last 12 timesteps × 50 members
    → state_caribbean.pkl (~50 MB)
  **SUCCESS** → STREAMSat_..._Ens50.nc
end note

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' WINDOW VISUALIZATION
' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

note bottom of out #E8EAF6
  <b>Time Window Visualization</b>
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  <color #C62828>▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓</color>  <color #1565C0>▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓</color>
  ← 12h warm-up →  ←────────── 48h output window (T−48h → T) ──────────→
  [ trimmed ]        [ ensemble QPE: 96 half-hourly steps ]
  
  Total ingest = 60h  |  Output = 48h (backward-looking, NOT forecast)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  <b>State persistence:</b> 12 overlapping timesteps saved per cycle
  → ensures member <i>k</i> at clock time <i>t</i> is bit-identical across cycles
end note

@enduml
